  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "The population of a diminishing bird species can be modelled using the equation\n\n$$A=A_0e^{-kt},$$\n\nwhere $A_0$ and $k$ are positive constants and $t$ is time in years. Initially, the population is 500. A year later, the population decreased down to 300.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $A_0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A_0=500$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}500&=A_0e^{-k(0)}\\\\500&=A_0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $k=\\ln\\left(\\frac53\\right)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=\\ln\\left(\\frac53\\right)$, using $A=300$ at $t=1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}300&=500e^{-k}\\\\e^{-k}&=\\frac35\\\\e^k&=\\frac53\\\\k&=\\ln\\left(\\frac53\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the population after ten years? Give your answer to the nearest whole bird.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "3 birds",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A(10)&=500e^{-10\\ln(5/3)}\\\\A(10)&=500\\left(\\frac35\\right)^{10}\\\\A(10)&=3.0233088.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis rounds to 3 birds.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "The bird species is considered extinct when the population is below 1. At the end of which year is the population first below 1?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "At the end of year 13.\n\nThe model reaches a population of 1 at about $12.17$ years.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}500e^{-kt}&<1\\\\e^{kt}&>500\\\\kt&>\\ln(500)\\\\t&>\\frac{\\ln(500)}{\\ln(5/3)}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $k>0$, the model decreases. The threshold is about $12.17$ years, so the first year-end with a population below 1 is at $t=13$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
